# AGENT VERIFICATION & WORKFLOW RULES

## 1. Automatic Task Verification
- NEVER mark a feature or task complete without verification.
- For backend changes: Run local test scripts and verify build status.
- For frontend changes: Launch the Browser Agent to inspect UI, verify interactions, and capture screenshot proof.
- Update `project_state.md` with build logs/test outcomes before finishing.

## 2. Multi-Agent & Parallel Execution Rules
- Before starting a multi-feature task, check for concurrent work.
- Always perform work in isolated branches or Git worktrees to avoid file conflicts across subagents.
- Ensure all merge requests run verification steps prior to merging back to `main`.

## 3. Project Memory Compliance
- Always read `ARCHITECTURE.md` before generating code to ensure consistency with project patterns.
- Always maintain `project_state.md` to track current progress and pending capstone tasks.
